    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 274,
      "topLeftY": 614,
      "bottomRightX": 642,
      "bottomRightY": 634,
      "content": "$$\\psi_n^{(2)} = \\chi_{ns}^{(0)}\\phi_n^{(2)} + \\chi_{ns}^{(1)}\\phi_n^{(1)} + \\chi_{ns}^{(2)}\\phi_n^{(0)}, \\tag{50}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 74,
      "topLeftY": 640,
      "bottomRightX": 595,
      "bottomRightY": 656,
      "content": "where $\\chi_{ns}^{(2)}$ denotes a new, undetermined function of the $\\zeta_i, \\theta_i$; this is easily verified using the identities (25).",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 74,
      "topLeftY": 659,
      "bottomRightX": 644,
      "bottomRightY": 691,
      "content": "We now consider the approximation equation of 3rd order (35d); after substitution of the already determined quantities, this becomes:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 205,
      "topLeftY": 702,
      "bottomRightX": 642,
      "bottomRightY": 768,
      "content": "$$\\begin{array}{l} \\left(H_0^{(0)} - V_n^{(0)}\\right)\\psi_n^{(3)} = \\left(W^{(3)} - H_0^{(3)} - H_{\\zeta\\theta}^{(0)} - H_{\\zeta\\zeta}^{(1)}\\right)\\chi_{ns}^{(0)}\\phi_n^{(0)} \\\\ + \\quad \\left(W_{ns}^{(2)} - H_0^{(2)} - H_{\\zeta\\zeta}^{(0)}\\right)\\left(\\chi_{ns}^{(0)}\\phi_n^{(1)} + \\chi_{ns}^{(1)}\\phi_n^{(0)}\\right) \\\\ - \\quad H_0^{(1)}\\left(\\chi_{ns}^{(0)}\\phi_n^{(2)} + \\chi_{ns}^{(1)}\\phi_n^{(1)} + \\chi_{ns}^{(2)}\\phi_n^{(0)}\\right). \\end{array} \\tag{51}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 74,
      "topLeftY": 779,
      "bottomRightX": 440,
      "bottomRightY": 795,
      "content": "We may consider the right-hand side as a development in the $\\phi_n^{(0)}$; we write",
